<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">affixes</ansi>

An affix is one special property on a piece of gear, from a prefix or suffix
in its name ("Mighty", "of the Bear"). An item has at most one affix of a
kind, so nothing rolls +Strength twice. What an affix can be depends on the
slot: weapons, shields, armor and jewelry each have their own pool.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What affixes do today</ansi>

  Stats        +Strength, Speed, Smarts, Vitality, Mysticism, Perception
  Vitals       +maximum health, +maximum mana
  Offense      +damage on every hit (weapons)
  Defense      +protection (armor and shields), +parry (weapons)
  Healing      +healing percent (weapons and jewelry)
  Logistics    +warmth (armor), -weight percent

An affix's size grows with the item's item level (<ansi fg="command">help itemlevel</ansi>). More chances,
resists, status-on-crit and the major mechanics (cleaving, vampiric,
warded, echoing) join as the systems that read them arrive.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Major affixes</ansi>

An Epic item has one major affix, a large one. For now majors are big
numbers: a strength of a Titan, Ironbound protection, Lifeblood health,
Saintly healing.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Seeing them</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">look [item]</ansi> lists an identified item's affixes. Unidentified gear hides
them (<ansi fg="command">help identify</ansi>) and gives nothing from them until it is read.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help rarity</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help quality</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help itemlevel</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help scribe</ansi>.
